# Data artifacts from local testing
git/
local_files/
raw_local_files/
websites/

# Real ServiceNow ticket data — operator-local only, never commit.
examples/benchmarking/snow_ragas_queries_pt1.json

# config/ is its own git repository (fasrc/archi-config, private) and holds
# config/benchmarking/secrets.env; committing it would either break as a
# gitlink or leak the secret. Deploys provision it automatically at a pinned,
# SHA-verified ref — see ensure_config in deploy/fasrc-dev/scripts/lib.sh.
/config/

# Claude Code session state (worktrees, plans, memory, local settings).
# Ignore everything under .claude/ EXCEPT project-authored agents — shared,
# archi-specific subagents are institutional knowledge worth versioning. The
# worktrees (full repo checkouts), settings.local.json, and runtime locks stay out.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/agents/

# Ralph harness runtime state (machine-written; never committed)
.ralph/
# The loop's task-list pointer (ralph.conf: RALPH_TASKS="tasks.md") is a SYMLINK to
# whichever OpenSpec change is active, so its target differs on every branch. While
# it was tracked, each branch had its own version and they conflicted with each
# other; ca31e80d (#164) dropped it from dev, which turned it into a modify/delete
# conflict that made five open PRs unmergeable at once (#159-#163, cleared under
# #168). It is working-tree state, so ignore it rather than track it. The leading
# slash is load-bearing: it anchors to the repo root, leaving the real
# openspec/changes/**/tasks.md files — the actual source of truth — tracked. Both
# properties are asserted by tests/unit/test_repo_hygiene.py.
/tasks.md
/review-findings.md
.coverage
coverage.xml

# FASRC 'dev' deployment. Track the secret-free orchestration scripts and a
# sanitized example config so the deploy is reproducible and not bus-factor-1,
# but keep the real host-specific config, agent prompts, source manifests, and
# any secrets out. Default-deny: a future stray file under deploy/fasrc-dev/ is
# ignored unless explicitly allow-listed here.
deploy/fasrc-dev/*
!deploy/fasrc-dev/scripts
!deploy/fasrc-dev/config.example.yaml
# Defense-in-depth: never track secrets/env even under the allow-listed scripts dir.
deploy/fasrc-dev/scripts/**/*.env
deploy/fasrc-dev/scripts/**/*secret*
